{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own","id":429027,"title":"E2 my thoughts (please share your own)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T11:13:06-08:00","id":429027,"title":"E2 my thoughts (please share your own)","content":"okay bought the book last night, gave it a quick read and chucks of it got a more thorough go between now and then.<br /> my thoughts? little underwhelmed;<br /> <br /> I'm really against it being a standalone book, there is about 44 pages of basic rules that could have been used for real content. the pure and hosts are practically absent and as always spirits need more fluff. 44 for pages of rules i own in three other books is a waste at best and an intentional means to bulk up the book with out writing anything new at worst. <br /> About a third of the art is recycled, annoying but whatever all the new art is great. <br /> it's not all bad by any means the big change ie the gift system is fantastic. How rites and fetishes are presented along with their practical usefulness are also way up there as my favourite part of the book. <br /> love the new harmony system it's simple, original and make sense.<br /> Tribes and auspices; the write ups are clearer with less problematic overlap, Signs/Tribes of the Moon fills the word count for content, where this book lacks.<br /> and again the lifelong problem with books word count is lower then I'd like covering the five forms and shapeshifting, but i do like the new form bonuses.<br /> seemingly scattered throughout the book (and of course the appendix) is a focus on large packs potentially filled with not just werewolves but wolf-blooded, spirits, animals, and normal both people knowing and unknowing. that really does inflate the idea of werewolves as a culture. which as a concept seems to dip up and down through out all the different books. <br /> now what I'd jump to comparing it to is Blood and Smoke and the first Werewolf book. And it's no Blood and Smoke by any means but it does manage to stand as a good replacement for E1 werewolf core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:21:49-08:00","id":429148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own#post429027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really against it being a standalone book, there is about 44 pages of basic rules that could have been used for real content. the pure and hosts are practically absent and as always spirits need more fluff. 44 for pages of rules i own in three other books is a waste at best and an intentional means to bulk up the book with out writing anything new at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only read through the &quot;common core&quot; rules a bit yesterday (rest of the book obviously got more attention), but it has a few differences from Requiem 2E's common rules section, like the details on spirits, i.e. the last 19 of those 44 pages are new.<br /> I understand your point however, but it's largely an unsolvable problem. If they require a core book, people who want to try out the world of darkness might be a bit put off by the requirement of an extra purchase (people often see things like that as a money grab) and then there would be complaints about the franchise being unfriendly to new players.<br /> <br /> As for the book itself, I never really played werewolf too much outside of two once off sessions, they just showed up as NPCs in Vampire or Mage games I've played/ran. However I am very excited to play this edition, much more than the first edition for the following reasons (note: I have not read the werewolf supplements much, this is 1E core vs 2E core):<br /> <br /> (a) The purpose of the five forms is much clearer to me from the text and the mechanics.They're a good bit beyond the +n stuff of before. I particularly mean the Urshul and Urhan forms here. Before I thought &quot;little wolf&quot;, &quot;big wolf&quot;, but the roles of &quot;chaser&quot; and &quot;harrier&quot; are much more evocative.<br /> EDIT: The Gauru form really benefits from the 2E combat, fights being resolved with the Down and Dirty rules really give the impression of an absolute monster.<br /> <br /> (b) The book is brutal. Werewolves aren't spirit police, but violent predators with five bodies and often a strong sense of justice. This is a general second edition improvement, the writing is fresher in the God Machine, Demon and Vampire 2E as well.<br /> <br /> (c) The Idigam are a fantastic bad guy. A clear narrative purpose, terrifying and several possible origins that simultaneously make sense, would be worth exploring and are not mutual exclusive.<br /> <br /> (d) The nineteen pages on spirits I mentioned above actually clarify their world and behaviour for me.<br /> <br /> \u200b(e) Purely emotional: The cover!<br /> <br /> I'm still digesting the Auspices and Gifts (that's my homework for today <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 03-05-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T12:52:01-08:00","id":429178,"title":"","content":"I really wish the Pure got more meat to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:09:43-08:00","id":429198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own#post429027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About a third of the art is recycled, annoying but whatever all the new art is great.<br /> it's not all bad by any means the big change ie the gift system is fantastic. How rites and fetishes are presented along with their practical usefulness are also way up there as my favourite part of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only four pieces of art were from previous Werewolf books, one each from four artists we wanted in the book but for various reasons they were unavailable. Thanks-<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:26:49-08:00","id":429215,"title":"","content":"Coming from Blood and Smoke to WtF 2e is a little jarring. I'd like to play it with a group before I have any final thoughts, but there seems to be a few things off in my opinion. <br /> <br /> First of all, the gifts and facets seem a bit disjointed in my eyes. Unlike in Blood and Smoke, where disciplines follow a clear progression, it seems more like gifts are just a bunch of assorted tricks under one theme, with only a few of them being powerful or useful. They seem interesting at first glance, but from reading a bit deeper into them they just seem mediocre.<br /> <br /> Second, I feel like that characters are going to be homogenized a bit. This may not be a factor in other groups, but mine seems to be &quot;all combat, all the time, plus humor.&quot; I feel like if I do play WtF 2E with my group, we're going to get at least 2-3 Rahu Blood Talons maxing out on brawl and Strength so they can kill whatever comes their way in werewolf form. <br /> <br /> Third, the power level in general seems to be lower than in Blood and Smoke. It seems like Werewolves get just as many weaknesses as Vampires without the benefit of becoming super strong or super fast or being able to control minds or whatever. Werewolves seem to be reigned in far more, and I'm unsure if my group will go for that.<br /> <br /> I'm probably on the extreme end of the spectrum when it comes to players/groups interested in WoD, but this sort of thing should be talked about, in my opinion at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:33:01-08:00","id":429225,"title":"","content":"&quot;Werewolves are weak spectrum&quot; <br /> <br /> And werewolves have a form that allows them to heal all Bashing and Lethal every turn, gain the equivalent of Vigor 3 (or was it +4?) and other such potent gifts? To to mention claws, and teeth. I'm not seeing 'weak'. And the Gift of Elements is really, really flexible. That doesn't seem weak. To me, it seems Werewolves got a big upgrade in power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:55:25-08:00","id":429257,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is fantastic and a great start in a new direction. It might seem rougher around the edges for many I think, but that might be because Werewolf is a game that needs more pages for everything.<br /> <br /> Everything written in this second edition has improved and advanced Werewolf as a game line. I can't wait to see more details in the future about Werewolves antagonists and how different Tribes or Packs perform their Sacred Hunts.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to future supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:05:46-08:00","id":429287,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've been really loud about how excited I was for the settings in this book, and my hype was <i>totally</i> justified. Basra came out of nowhere, but is a fascinating sandbox. Alice Springs is somewhere I could totally see myself setting a chronicle. But one of the cities takes the cake: Tokyo. Just... that Tokyo setting! That <i>Tengu</i> sidebar! I haven't stopped screaming since I saw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:08:43-08:00","id":429290,"title":"","content":"My only complaint right now is that I want fully fleshed out 2e Pure and the additional Auspice and Tribe Gifts of the Forsaken (Alpha, Ending, Stalking, Adaptation, and Battle)...<br /> <br /> I want them NOW!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:11:59-08:00","id":429292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429290#post429290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaint right now is that I want fully fleshed out 2e Pure and the additional Auspice and Tribe Gifts of the Forsaken (Alpha, Ending, Stalking, Adaptation, and Battle)...<br /> <br /> I want them NOW!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 2e Pure is definitely at the top of my wanted list now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:18:05-08:00","id":429296,"title":"","content":"Whilst I'm all for more material I feel upon reading the core I have enough to run those antagonists, and I do have access to the 1st ed fluff stuff as well. The core book is way more complete and tight than first edition was, which is awesome.<br /> <br /> The Idigam are terrifyingly cool, my new favourite monsters. The chapter at the back of Night Horrors look paltry in comparison xD<br /> <br /> The bit in the spirit section mentioning heralds of Spirit Gods. Thank you very much, working those gods down into a game is very doable now. Can't wait for a PC to meet their Tribal Totem, or at least a reflection of it.<br /> <br /> The Drowned got a mention! Woop! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:30:01-08:00","id":429302,"title":"","content":"Dreaminggod, I realize that they probably got an increase in power, however, I didn't play first edition, so I have no prior experience to base that assumption off of. <br /> <br /> Besides that, I'm simply saying that I think Vampires get off in the more interesting and powerful direction with their disciplines compared to Werewolves and their Gifts. The Gangrel I'm currently playing in my groups off-and-on Blood and Smoke campaign can seemingly do a lot of the same things that a werewolf can do but even better because his abilities scale as I continue to play him. <br /> <br /> I will agree with you that the Gift of the Elementals is quite awesome, and I plan on making my first WtF 2E character utilize it. I just wish it, and Influence in general had a bit more fleshing out on how to use it in different situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:32:18-08:00","id":429306,"title":"","content":"I understand what people are talking about in regards to stuff they wanted to see, but for me, WtF was about coming back to the basics and the original characters, the central characters of the line, and bringing them up to snuff, alongside the ideas that were initially presented with them. Second Edition made me fall in love not only with Forsaken all over again(Which is sort of saying something, since Forsaken brought me in but it was Created and Lost that made me fall in love with WoD), but with werewolves in general, which was a cornerstone of my youth, so yay.<br /> <br /> It really comes back to when I called it unapologetic. Forsaken has had less of identity crisis then Requiem, as shown through the stellar ideas in the supplements, but now it's brought forward and center stage, it's been sharpened and clarified, and most importantly it's had an injection of cool and sexy alongside the visceral and brutal nature of the game. It does not give a shit and stands solidly as it's own beast, and looks legitimately fun in a way the first edition core kind of missed out on.<br /> <br /> Is it perfect? Maybe not, but I'm more excited for Werewolf the Forsaken than I have been in years, and that's all I wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:37:19-08:00","id":429309,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly... a little disappointed?<br /> <br /> I felt that there was too much room given over to the Idigam, instead of stuff like the Shartha who are will probably end up being used more often. I mean, sure, have them in there (it <i>was</i> going to be called the Idigam Chronicles, after all), but I don't think we needed to have <i>five</i> of them in the core, with each getting 5+ pages. I would have been happy with just three of them (probably dropping the last two) and more pages dedicated to building the different Prey; heck, even just having the Idigam section be &quot;here's how you go from an idea for an Idigam to a fully fleshed out one!&quot;<br /> <br /> The art felt like it was poorly distributed throughout the book; I think the Idigam section should have gotten more art (especially for the False Father, who I have a bit of trouble visualizing), while some of the art in amongst the Gifts felt... out of place?<br /> <br /> I can't complain about the mechanics for <i>Werewolves</i>; however, I feel that the Dread Powers should have either been called something else, or they should have had dot ratings. As it stands, they are a different beast than Hunter Dread Powers, which I think is kinda confusing.<br /> <hr /><br /> To bring up a comparison to Blood and Smoke, the only reason that book got away with focusing so much on the Strix was because Vampires have a &quot;simpler&quot; ecology; you've got Humans, Ghouls, Vampires, and Strix. Done. You can <i>afford</i> to give each group their own section, because there are four of them, and one of those is just the default.<br /> <br /> Same for Demon; you've got Humans, Angels, Demons, Stigmatics, and Cryptids. Really, that's more like Angels, Demons, and Cryptids, since Stigmatics are just a really simple template you can slap on a Human.<br /> <br /> For Werewolf, you've gotta cover Werewolves, Spirits, Claimed, Hosts, Humans, Wolfblooded, and Idigam. Information on more common foes (the Pure, Hosts, Claimed...) was cut in deference to the Idigam, where you're going to have maybe two of them in a Chronicle, if you are <i>really</i> stretching things. And the thing is? You can't really use the ones in the book for full effect if your players have also read the book.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, they're an out-of-context problem, so you have to be ingenious in how you deal with them; however, that's exactly why I think too much wordcount was spent on them. A section that <i>walked you through</i> the process of creating an Idigam would have ultimately been more helpful.<br /> <hr />In summary:<br /> <br /> 1. I feel too much wordcount was spent on the Idigam.<br /> 2. Not enough wordcount was spent on Prey other than Spirits.<br /> 3. The art didn't feel like it was well-distributed.<br /> 4. Otherwise, the rules were good.<br /> 5. I can't comment on either the Hunting Grounds or the stories, because that kinda stuff isn't really in my field of interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:39:43-08:00","id":429311,"title":"","content":"One of the little things I'm glad to see is that the sole exception to the core Gift affinities carrying over from 1e is the Hirfathra Hissu and the Meninna swapping Elemental and Warding Gifts into their respective lists (and not just because those are arguably better conceptual fits, either; Elodoth Bone Shadows had the smallest affiliated affinity spread in 1e because of the identical satellite affinities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:06:50-08:00","id":429327,"title":"","content":"I'm annoyed that Hunter's Aspect doesn't talk about other Aura mechanics at all, like Blood and Smoke did. By RAW, a vampire can sense a werewolf but not visa versa, and a vampire can defend against a hunter's aspect with predatory aura but it doesn't say for sure if a werewolf can do likewise. It was a tiny sidebar, too, it's not like it'd kill wordcount...<br /> <br /> Beyond that though, I really love it so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:15:33-08:00","id":429334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429198#post429198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only four pieces of art were from previous Werewolf books, one each from four artists we wanted in the book but for various reasons they were unavailable. Thanks-<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course things like this happen and they have to be dealt with, using art onyx path already owns is pragmatic.<br /> but on the flip side it reminds me that I would drop a comic that reused old art intermittently and I can't think of a reason not to hold Onyx Path up to the same standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:18:39-08:00","id":429336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shomaxt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429215#post429215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming from Blood and Smoke to WtF 2e is a little jarring. I'd like to play it with a group before I have any final thoughts, but there seems to be a few things off in my opinion.<br /> <br /> First of all, the gifts and facets seem a bit disjointed in my eyes. Unlike in Blood and Smoke, where disciplines follow a clear progression, it seems more like gifts are just a bunch of assorted tricks under one theme, with only a few of them being powerful or useful. They seem interesting at first glance, but from reading a bit deeper into them they just seem mediocre.<br /> <br /> Second, I feel like that characters are going to be homogenized a bit. This may not be a factor in other groups, but mine seems to be &quot;all combat, all the time, plus humor.&quot; I feel like if I do play WtF 2E with my group, we're going to get at least 2-3 Rahu Blood Talons maxing out on brawl and Strength so they can kill whatever comes their way in werewolf form.<br /> <br /> Third, the power level in general seems to be lower than in Blood and Smoke. It seems like Werewolves get just as many weaknesses as Vampires without the benefit of becoming super strong or super fast or being able to control minds or whatever. Werewolves seem to be reigned in far more, and I'm unsure if my group will go for that.<br /> <br /> I'm probably on the extreme end of the spectrum when it comes to players/groups interested in WoD, but this sort of thing should be talked about, in my opinion at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the first things I want to look for two primary reasons. 1. Werewolf the Forsaken 1st edition left the Uratha in somewhat of a bad spot when compared to other game lines. While game lines are not, and should not, be balanced against each other. Even in context of just Werewolf many folks commented on how there were too many lackluster gifts. 2. On the other hand I don't want to relive Werewolf the Apocalypse and my hope is the overall potency of the splat isn't pushed too far in 2e.<br /> <br /> But most of all I want it to be interesting. 1st edition left me cold with it's somewhat bland tribe descriptions,etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T15:20:12-08:00","id":429338,"title":"","content":"I think the Sheeps' Clothing effect of Hishu form would probably dull the sensing effect. And Werewolves can easily switch to wolf senses and notice things like a lack of heartbeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:17:39-08:00","id":429403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429334#post429334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course things like this happen and they have to be dealt with, using art onyx path already owns is pragmatic.<br /> but on the flip side it reminds me that I would drop a comic that reused old art intermittently and I can't think of a reason not to hold Onyx Path up to the same standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a) you did not lose out on any new art, we added those 4 pieces specifically because we wanted those artists to be represented in 2nd Edition as they were some of the best guys in 1st. And b) you're comparing apples to oranges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:30:01-08:00","id":429416,"title":"","content":"Does &quot;Primal Form&quot; not exist anymore? Or maybe it's being saved for the Predator Kings Gifts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:44:36-08:00","id":429471,"title":"","content":"Primal Form does not exist any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:25:07-08:00","id":429505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429471#post429471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Form does not exist any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I won't be surprised if it comes back as. Predator King gift... That's what I'd do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:31:03-08:00","id":429508,"title":"","content":"To be Lear, I realize Rahu's stronger regeneration means that aspect of Primal Form wouldn't necessarily come back, but the tank sized wolf form is a cool threat niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T17:58:28-08:00","id":429525,"title":"","content":"The only complaint I had from my couple-hour perusal was that the sample idigam didn't really hook me like the ones in <b>Wolfsbane</b>, but mostly I think that section could've used some more artwork. The whole idigam section just felt like a giant wall of text to me.<br /> <br /> Actually, the whole book kind seems like a wall of text. I'm still kinda confused on starting gifts and such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:38:42-08:00","id":429574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429525#post429525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only complaint I had from my couple-hour perusal was that the sample idigam didn't really hook me like the ones in <b>Wolfsbane</b>, but mostly I think that section could've used some more artwork. The whole idigam section just felt like a giant wall of text to me.<br /> <br /> Actually, the whole book kind seems like a wall of text. I'm still kinda confused on starting gifts and such</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You start with the first dot of your moon, gift, you get a facet of two shadow gifts from either your tribal gift list or auspice gift list (based on renown), if you have two dots in your auspice renown you get the second dot there, otherwise you get a wolf gift facet for one of your three renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:50:17-08:00","id":429599,"title":"","content":"I like the gift/facet design quite a bit. Now, if two werewolves have different different emphases on renown, then even if they have the same gift, it will work differently. <br /> Starting gifts make sense to me thanks to the little sidebar on the character reference page, but I have no idea how many rites starting characters get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:51:35-08:00","id":429601,"title":"","content":"2 dots in rites, so 2 one dot rites or 1 two dot rite<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T20:10:46-08:00","id":429654,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">To begin, I absolutely love W:tF. It's my favorite game line and will always be. I'm really glad that 2nd ed is out and i'm sure that all of my players can attest to my rampant checking of the website for any shred of an update. Thank you OP for delivering this book.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">That being said, my reflection on this book is a mixed bag. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The rules update is wonderful. Many of the systems are streamlined and plenty of quality of life improvements that I think are a great addition to the game. The Gifts are great(especially with the facet system) however, there are still a few that I just don't think are worth their weight in salt or simply seem out of place (Maw of Madness I'm looking at you). I like a lot of the fun new powers that the Uratha have access to, including all of the new Auspice powers and the forms are in perfect Harmony.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Unfortunately, I'm not a fan of the new art. The full color chapter dividers don't really scream werewolf and aren\u2019t nearly as evocative of the setting as Ron Spencer's art did in the 1st Ed book. The man is quite possibly the best artist any of the werewolf books have ever seen (including W:tA) and more of his work being featured on a full page layout would have done some good. As it is, the new art doesn\u2019t really hold a torch to any of the previous pieces in the 1st edition books. I am glad that some of the art from the core book was reused since its just as good as the day it was released. I realize that some of artists that were originally requested were unable to make deadlines or just didn't respond and that's not Onyx Path's fault.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The emphasis on the hunt and the sheer brutality that is laced in this book is great. It gets you amped up as you read it and you can really feel the pull of a predator's instinct. I like this addition but I also feel that with this theme being so dominant it snuffs out the savage nobility and duty-bound nature that was at the forefront of the Forsaken culture in previous books. 2nd edition feels like it is trying to move away from the &quot;Spirit Cops&quot; feel in favor of promoting &quot;the Hunt&quot; which I understand but is just a shift in emphasis for me.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The community gave some great feedback over the course of this book's development and I think that we could have given even greater feedback to the authors if perhaps we would have gotten an early release similar to how V:tR did &quot;Reap the Whirlwind&quot;. I really liked this approach and it generated new interest in V:tR for me when it was released.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">All in all, I'm still glad that the book was released as I've been dying to start my game with a blank slate so, thank you very much! </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4590-handriel","user":"Handriel","date":". 03-05-2015, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4590-handriel","name":"Handriel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4590_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T20:22:52-08:00","id":429692,"title":"","content":"May I take a second to say that the nobility aspect has shifted soundly onto Renown, and well it should. Werewolves don't think that being a werewolf, an engine of violence and predation, is inherently a noble thing, and they're right-which is why it's tied to the virtues of Renown and prompts Werewolves to be more than just those engines. It's still not a wholly ....moral thing, but there's nobility to be found in crafting one's self as an Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",