d":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T20:55:27-08:00","id":429770,"title":"","content":"Yeah I had a similar issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T02:27:00-08:00","id":429962,"title":"","content":"Is all the fluff in the 1st edition werewolf books still relevant to 2nd edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/500-rindel","name":"Rindel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T04:40:39-08:00","id":430019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429525#post429525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only complaint I had from my couple-hour perusal was that the sample idigam didn't really hook me like the ones in <b>Wolfsbane</b>, but mostly I think that section could've used some more artwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a side-note, the Wolfsbane idigam should still be fairly compatible with the new system, I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T04:42:16-08:00","id":430021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rindel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429962#post429962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is all the fluff in the 1st edition werewolf books still relevant to 2nd edition</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of it, no. For example, with the removal of <i>unihar</i>, a certain amount of the 1st edition content around uratha mating and <i>unihar</i> is obviously now out of date.<br /> <br /> The vast bulk can still be used just fine with 2nd edition, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:11:06-08:00","id":430144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429692#post429692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I take a second to say that the nobility aspect has shifted soundly onto Renown, and well it should. Werewolves don't think that being a werewolf, an engine of violence and predation, is inherently a noble thing, and they're right-which is why it's tied to the virtues of Renown and prompts Werewolves to be more than just those engines. It's still not a wholly ....moral thing, but there's nobility to be found in crafting one's self as an Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes a lot of sense. When you put it that way it more or less clears up that point of contention that I had. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4590-handriel","name":"Handriel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4590_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:30:52-08:00","id":430190,"title":"","content":"My first impressions of Second Edition:<br /> <br /> I have a deep love for Werewolf. Werewolf the Apocalypse 2 edition was one of my first books for Roleplaying. Then came revised edition, and New world of darkness with the Forsaken. tIt has been a long and fantastic ride.<br /> each time Werewolf changes, I find the game opens new sides to tell stories. It has a long evolution and it is an evolution Im happy to have told some stories in.<br /> <br /> Man, im getting older!<br /> Before we get all emotional, lets get to impressions!<br /> <br /> The Good:<br /> * The written content is top-notch. Some errors to be fixed before physical book-release, no biggie.<br /> * The material offers a solid update to the GMC system rues changes.<br /> * I like that the material focuses on Uratha. Pure were meant as antagonists and I dont need a book to run them as NPC's. As for playing them? well 1st edition did not have playable Pure from the get go either.<br /> * New Gift system looks great, but I need to test it in-game to give verdict.<br /> * Tribe and Auspice update was simple, well put together. Easy to use.<br /> * Pack structure! I knew this was coming, but this changes the ball-game for me. Again: i must play-test this.<br /> * Harmony<br /> * Wolf blooded! This was maybe one of the most anticipated parts of the new book for my sake. It was all I wanted. it felt like it was short, but at the same time it took full use of its ages to be as informative and useful as possible. Well done! We are playing with wolf-blooded now and some of the tells are similar to what we are playing with already. they will be converted to the book standard as we play onwards.<br /> <br /> The Bad:<br /> * The Artwork was sadly very uneven.<br /> I liked the wolf shown in all its dread as a full page color (Brian Le Blanc I believe).<br /> This was perhaps the picture that struck me the most.<br /> I also liked the Tribe picture of the female Imnir. Dreads and Gauru cant go wrong!<br /> Some pictures were from the old edition. I know that some artists did not make it in with new art this time around.<br /> Hopefully some of them can deliver new work for the physical book release on Drive-thru?<br /> The auspice artwork was not to my tastes. The pictures had some composition-issues. One of them reminds me of a very good picture in 1 edition (Uratha vs Azlu). this can be issues I have with style and how I feel, but the new picture is too close to the one in 1 edition (white background, single battle between Azlu and Uratha).<br /> Some of the full-pagers looked more like Shadowrun than Werewolf and felt rushed, or like there was a bit of uncertainty on what would fit the layout.<br /> <br /> * Spirit Flowchart is back! I'm so sorry, but I really don't like this thing. Keep it simple!<br /> <br /> * The Idigam are still an impossible foe to relate to.<br /> Even though the Idigam are fascinating, they are not really the meat of this book.<br /> I think the material worked well to build on the excellent Wolfsbane material, and build &quot;the big bad&quot; mood. <br /> And that is kind of it: Idigam will always be that one shot enemy you put in the background.<br /> The Shartha, The Pure, The Bale Hounds, hunters, spirits and humans would all be more interesting to explore in-depth for their drives and motivations.<br /> You will far more often face these foes than the Idigam. Especially in a brutal and savage game that invites you to investigate the insides of raging beasts and what makes them tick.<br /> I know that WtF 2nd ed was envisioned not as full book but as a chronicle book for the Idigam. As the process went, I'm glad this turned into a full blown 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Sum up:<br /> In general from what I have read and skimmed over, this book hits the ball out of the park for me.<br /> The written material is strong and discuss the Uratha re-imagined for a new edition and makes me hungry to build on my running WtF game. Players have more than enought to keep them occupied, as their roles are evolved with onset of GMC game-rules. this is good as it gives both players and Storyteller the time to mesh their game in a way that everyone wants to play.<br /> Storytelling-parts of the book gives me ideas and inspiration for future stories and games.<br /> I feel like I will be playing a lot of Werewolf in the future and Im happy that the book is refueling my interest in one of 1st editions finest games. 1st edition had some flaws (among them Unihar and the lack of enpowered wolfblooded). It is good to see the game opening up and showing more of the insides. More guts.. Actually the game is now far more brutal. the focus on Kuruth and the fury inside make uratha a ticking bomb. The game wants the players to let loose the beast. unleash chaos. The Werewolves are hungry.<br /> This is a game that wants players to know the headaches of consequences and how it is to play very unstable beings in a world where they are also the apex predator.<br /> <br /> The pack structure is less about the Uratha now. Wolfblooded come in and take up some space. This lets the players play different games. Wolfblooded or Uratha. both have implications for what you do in the pack. I also like the focus on letting humans support the pack more directly than before. Someone has been watching a lot of Sons of Anarchy!<br /> <br /> Some portons (like the Idigam) have less to give for a story than more mature topics that come from Uratha interaction with humans and spirits. This is nitpicking from my side.<br /> <br /> I think the artwork is suffering from a time-crunch here and there. There are parts that glimmer, but sadly this is not the best drawn wolves I've seen.<br /> <br /> The book is worth a buy if you are till on the fence. If you have wanted to upgrade your Werewolf game to new edition, this is a good one folks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:28:12-08:00","id":430246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=429702#post429702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character also begins play with two dots in rites.<br /> These are detailed further on p. 138.<br /> <br /> page 83, the last full sentence in Gifts and Rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. The quick-glance character creation table could use that one, as someone said I think<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=430019#post430019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side-note, the Wolfsbane idigam should still be fairly compatible with the new system, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had assumed it'd be similar enough. I was just saying that none were like, &quot;This could be my campaign's BBEG right fucking now&quot; like a couple were from the <b>Night Horrors</b> book...<br /> <br /> ...BUT I hope, and honestly expect, my mind to change in favor of them once I can really dig into that section <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> all the writers did a great job and I haven't seen any glaring issues that make me regret my purchase or that would deter me from playing it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 03-06-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:39:13-08:00","id":430796,"title":"","content":"I do have to wonder why we got two idigam who both want their own Tribes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:50:37-08:00","id":430808,"title":"","content":"I do have to wonder why Relentless Assault is Uratha-only; I'm kinda curious why it's not also available to, say, Wolf-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T21:25:36-08:00","id":431036,"title":"","content":"Wanting to support Onyx Path, and being an old hand from Werewolf in the CWoD days I picked up the pdf last night. I skimmed over it, really liking the art. But for now no capacity to make a judgement until I sit and read it. Also new to the 2e system so it's going to be a little while to digest it and understand it. While somewhat nervous over power issues I am really looking forward to reading the Gifts section as I felt 1e Gifts were so underwhelming and the new Auspice and Tribe descriptions as both felt a little bland to me in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T03:00:12-08:00","id":431162,"title":"","content":"In terms of pure system and rules, I believe it's quite simply a better game than its first edition. There are things I don't like, but if you consider it in its entirety, it's better. Flaws in the rules of the first edition have been fixed. The power level of the protagonists is where it should be. So that's a big plus. <br /> <br /> In terms of setting and its representation, it's different from its first edition, in ways I mostly don't like. <br /> <br /> It's like this - the first edition of the game is a horror game. It's established right in the corebook that I have in front of me right now - the Forsaken are exactly that, Forsaken. There's a strong sense of desperation in the setting - the Forsaken have been outnumbered by the Pure ever since the Brethren War. The idigam are back. There's also plenty of elaboration of the downsides of being a werewolf - the rage, the many things werewolves are afraid of, especially about themselves. <br /> <br /> The 2nd edition book doesn't spend too much time talking about that. The protagonists of the second edition don't have it that hard. There are gaps in the storytelling section of the book, a section that, in my opinion, should really address the downsides of the Forsaken condition, and, again in my opinion, fails to do so. <br /> <br /> Examples: <br /> The Iron Masters hunt people. Think about this for a moment. They. Hunt. People. I find that to be a fantastic, evocative, thematically appropriate idea! Except that the book doesn't spend any word count at all on elaborating on in, presenting it in any sort of context or how scary, frightening a notion this is. <br /> <br /> Expanded packs - wolf-blooded and people can now be a part of packs. The reason I don't like it is because it destroys part of the sense of desperation and isolation of the setting. In the first edition, it's just you and the other werewolves you call a pack. There's noone else you can rely on. Human interaction is hard, people cannot ever understand what it's like to be Forsaken. This is part of the horror of the setting - you're alone, yet the Uratha must still cleave to the human, because you cannot help being drawn to the world you came from. In 2nd edition, there's less of a thematic space for this sort of dramatic tension, because you get to have people as part of your pack. The Forsaken are less Forsaken because of that. <br /> <br /> I dislike the termination of the unihar as a concept for a similar reason - it decreases the Forsaken factor. In first edition, if you lie with your own kind, you beget a monster. If you lie with humans, your relationship is almost certainly doomed to fail. In second edition, all that is gone. <br /> <br /> It's a matter of personal taste, obviously - but the implications of the unihar never bothered me. This is supposed to be a horror and drama game; and there's plenty of drama in the notion of people who cannot ever be together and intimate with the only people who are like them and who know what it's like. <br /> <br /> And then there's the tone - I far too often catch myself thinking that 2nd edition presents its protagonists in a glorifying, celebratory light that didn't exist in the first edition. The book emphasizes the upsides of the werewolf condition in ways that make me uncomfortable at times. It shouldn't be great to be a werewolf. It shouldn't be great to experience the rage and the hunger for flesh and the desire to hunt. The first edition of the game doesn't suffer from this particular problem. Blood and Smoke, a game that I like better than the first edition of Vampire, really absolutely doesn't suffer from this particular problem. <br /> <br /> It would be wrong to say that Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd edition isn't well written, doesn't have great rules and isn't coherent in terms of its themes and mood. I must applaud the writers and the developer for their work - more Werewolf books are always good, and I hope there's more coming. Still, speaking for my own tastes, I prefer the setting of the first edition. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T04:22:23-08:00","id":431252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431162#post431162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, speaking for my own tastes, I prefer the setting of the first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, you don't use the rules, anyway, but if you <i>did</i>, I think one thing that would be nice is it should be pretty easy to use the 2E rules with First Edition's setting. I know in my own games, I'm going to be emphasizing certain horror elements, too. It's a scary world out there. Werewolves are apex predators because they have to be, but the food chain that requires such predation is a nasty, dangerous affair. You are a monster hunting the monstrous, and every level should emphasize that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T04:45:15-08:00","id":431257,"title":"","content":"Correct on all counts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:07:19-08:00","id":431385,"title":"","content":"I think the horror element is still present in the setting, it's just not focused on in the writing as much. It's still horrifying when you take a moment to stop and think about the fact that your character, upon learning she was a monster (likely killing people in the process) sought out (or was sought out by) other monsters like her, who basically told her its normal and she should abandon her old life and human morality to join a cult that communes with spiritsvand religiously hunts and kills human beings. But to me personally, the 1e core book focused so much on that, it left me thinking &quot;so... WHY would I want to join these crazy people?&quot; The shift from regular Jill to horrible monster was too jarring for me to come up with a character I liked who would willingly go along with such a shit deal. 2e shows the up-side so you can identify more with the people who embrace Uratha culture, and let's you come to the realization of how horrifying that is on your own, just as your character might. It's more versimilar that way for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:12:12-08:00","id":431391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431162#post431162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Examples:<br /> The Iron Masters hunt people. Think about this for a moment. They. Hunt. People. I find that to be a fantastic, evocative, thematically appropriate idea! Except that the book doesn't spend any word count at all on elaborating on in, presenting it in any sort of context or how scary, frightening a notion this is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, this is exactly why I support the &quot;Tribes of the Moon&quot; petition for a series of tribe books. I don't know how much of it is the fact that I'm familiar with 1e stuff, but you can <i>feel</i> the ideas behind each Tribe being understated by their word count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:19:51-08:00","id":431423,"title":"","content":"The Horror is playing a character who can potentially go on a murder spree and feel <i>saner</i> afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:20:33-08:00","id":431426,"title":"","content":"You know Christian, given what I've read of 2e so far, I think you may have something of a point about the lack of gravitas on why the Uratha we play are called the <i>Forsaken</i>, and the over-glorification of the predator aspect. Maybe.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, highly subjective because.... horror is subjective. And in my opinion, there is a whole fantastic brand of horror in coming to the conclusion that the book, in many parts written semi-in character, <i>glorifies</i> what a normal person would look at as extremely disturbing. It doesn't lack horror because of its glorification. That glorification <i>is</i> what's horrifying.<br /> <br /> I have the impression what you might be describing is solely the horror from the perspective of an outsider. While a werewolf that just tore a person limb from limb would be <i>loving life</i>. And it's written as &quot;So I just tore a person limb from limb. <i>Goddamn I'm fucking alpha</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is genuinely fucking terrifying. And that is actually a very well done form of &quot;show, don't tell&quot;. The book doesn't speak to us about the horror. It <i>shows it to us</i>, by presenting the perspective of the werewolf. Instead of telling us what to feel, it allows us to make our own conclusions. In my opinion, it achieves its objectives quite nicely on that front.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, I'm not going to disagree that the book <i>could</i> have used more details and word count in certain aspects, such as each of the Prey, and overall situation of the Forsaken as often besieged from all sides by enemies. But it still does excellently with what it presents, and it manages to show everything vital to Werewolf The Forsaken in an appropriate manner. It's a tight and focused book that does what it set out to do, I would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-07-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:28:20-08:00","id":431451,"title":"","content":"I have not finished it entirely, but here are some bullet points (in no particular order):<ul><li>On the whole it seems like a significant improvement (coming from someone who is not an exceptionally big fan of WtF)</li> <li>I am slightly disappointed by the drier writing style compared to VtR 2e. The prose in VtR 2e is a terrific joy to read and I often find myself going back to reread the first and second chapter just to enjoy it again. I do not expect to have this happen much with WtF 2e.</li> <li>Related to the above: It sometimes seems to focus too much on the facts and too little on the feel, which seems odd considering how passionate Werewolves are.</li> <li>Most of the new rules seem pretty sweet. With some others I would need some more time to mull them over.</li> <li>New Gifts are actually cool and noteworthy.</li> <li>Some contradictions/unclear points/mechanical hiccups are a bit jarring, like the detection immunity in Hishu raised in another thread.</li> <li>Some very nice artwork, but somewhat uneven in later parts of the book (as has been said)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> As for Christian A's points raised above: As a bit of an outsider to WtF, I can certainly see where he is coming from. Things certainly do not feel as desperate and grim as in first edition. That being said, I am not sure that was not part of its Apocalypse DNA, which has now been purged. Unlike the Werewolves of Apocalypse, the Forsaken are not meant to eventually fail utterly. In all likelihood they will have to continue their hunt for all eternity (which might, in some way, be even worse), so there probably has to be some good with all the bad. Things like the extended pack make them seem more rooted in the World of Darkness as a whole.<br /> <br /> Of course, mood and theme are easily adjusted to one's particular tables, so it is an easy fix, whether one likes the new direction or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:05:06-08:00","id":431508,"title":"","content":"As someone whose primary beef with WtF is the perceived lack of inherent horror, I can echo the thought that 2e is weak in that regard. Ideas like &quot;you were never actually human&quot; and &quot;you can lose your humanity utterly and become an alien spirit&quot; are tossed in, but not given the wordcount they need to be sufficiently punchy.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the antagonists section needs a lot of love. Idigam are the likely Big Bad of a given chronicle, but two of them are far too similar (the Deceiver Lune and False Father both want Tribes of their own), and the bulk of a chronicle will go to fighting Spirits and Pure, who both got too little space in my eyes.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think Werewolf got a much weaker book than Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-07-2015, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:17:01-08:00","id":431528,"title":"","content":"Again, I take kind of the opposite tact. Werewolf didn't drown in its' tragedy the way Requiem did initially, but Forsaken had a heavy dose of misery throughout the book. It was manageable, but it could be a downer that turned people away from the game. <i>Changeling </i>reveled more in it's condition than the first Forsaken core, or at least more carefully balanced its' tragedy with its' beautiful madness approach to the book.<br /> <br /> I feel like Little Faith(I need a better way to shorten your name. Ye?) hits on what works. It starts with a sense that being a werewolf is awesome, and as it goes along it starts slipping in the reason being a werewolf sucks as discordant strings mixed in with it, creating a mixed feeling of power and revelry mixed in with alienating roughness and dire 'weights'. Sure, starting off the book feels like a power trip, but by the end there's something of that horizon feeling of an adrenalin rush-you still feel like you can do anything, but you can't shake off the feeling of a crash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:19:08-08:00","id":431531,"title":"","content":"Yolf or Faith work perfectly well as shortened forms, Arc!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:21:18-08:00","id":431533,"title":"","content":"Yolf is fun to say!<br /> <br /> Feels good on the tongue, you know?(Thank you, I'll be here all week)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:34:22-08:00","id":431569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431426#post431426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know Christian, given what I've read of 2e so far, I think you may have something of a point about the lack of gravitas on why the Uratha we play are called the <i>Forsaken</i>, and the over-glorification of the predator aspect. Maybe.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, highly subjective because.... horror is subjective. And in my opinion, there is a whole fantastic brand of horror in coming to the conclusion that the book, in many parts written semi-in character, <i>glorifies</i> what a normal person would look at as extremely disturbing. It doesn't lack horror because of its glorification. That glorification <i>is</i> what's horrifying.<br /> <br /> I have the impression what you might be describing is solely the horror from the perspective of an outsider. While a werewolf that just tore a person limb from limb would be <i>loving life</i>. And it's written as &quot;So I just tore a person limb from limb. <i>Goddamn I'm fucking alpha</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is genuinely fucking terrifying. And that is actually a very well done form of &quot;show, don't tell&quot;. The book doesn't speak to us about the horror. It <i>shows it to us</i>, by presenting the perspective of the werewolf. Instead of telling us what to feel, it allows us to make our own conclusions. In my opinion, it achieves its objectives quite nicely on that front.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, I'm not going to disagree that the book <i>could</i> have used more details and word count in certain aspects, such as each of the Prey, and overall situation of the Forsaken as often besieged from all sides by enemies. But it still does excellently with what it presents, and it manages to show everything vital to Werewolf The Forsaken in an appropriate manner. It's a tight and focused book that does what it set out to do, I would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say this is a good way of looking at it, overall.<br /> <br /> There's actually an anecdote here that I could share, but it would require sharing a line from the book's outline, and I'm not sure I can do that without getting in trouble. Stew? (If you're around?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:39:05-08:00","id":431579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431508#post431508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond that, the antagonists section needs a lot of love. Idigam are the likely Big Bad of a given chronicle, but two of them are far too similar (the Deceiver Lune and False Father both want Tribes of their own), and the bulk of a chronicle will go to fighting Spirits and Pure, who both got too little space in my eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claire and I actually had a chat about those two back when we conceptualized them, and the similarity (having an analog for both of the legendary progenitors) was intentional. I don't recall offhand if we specifically discussed tribes or not, though.<br /> <br /> Still, one might strike better chords in someone's chronicle than the other (and, judging from comments I've seen here and on RPG.net, it looks like Claire's is the more popular! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), so that's something to keep in mind. Or, again to the best of my recollection as I don't have the thing in front of me at the moment, I don't think either of them are particularly powerful on their own. There isn't anything saying you couldn't use both in a chronicle back behind the scenes. I mean, what would it do to the Forsaken if it appeared like both their Mother and their Father were no longer distant (or dead), but instead, actively engaging with the world?<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts, which may or may not appeal to anyone's given game. But maybe it'll strike up some ideas, so that's good at least. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:34:17-08:00","id":431649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431426#post431426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know Christian, given what I've read of 2e so far, I think you may have something of a point about the lack of gravitas on why the Uratha we play are called the <i>Forsaken</i>, and the over-glorification of the predator aspect. Maybe.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, highly subjective because.... horror is subjective. And in my opinion, there is a whole fantastic brand of horror in coming to the conclusion that the book, in many parts written semi-in character, <i>glorifies</i> what a normal person would look at as extremely disturbing. It doesn't lack horror because of its glorification. That glorification <i>is</i> what's horrifying.<br /> <br /> I have the impression what you might be describing is solely the horror from the perspective of an outsider. While a werewolf that just tore a person limb from limb would be <i>loving life</i>. And it's written as &quot;So I just tore a person limb from limb. <i>Goddamn I'm fucking alpha</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is genuinely fucking terrifying. And that is actually a very well done form of &quot;show, don't tell&quot;. The book doesn't speak to us about the horror. It <i>shows it to us</i>, by presenting the perspective of the werewolf. Instead of telling us what to feel, it allows us to make our own conclusions. In my opinion, it achieves its objectives quite nicely on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one half. The other half is the enemies as a whole simply can't be beaten by force alone. Hunt a spirit and now it's counterparts has claimed your wife until you call off the hunt. Friends and family who are largely powerless are at the mercy of spirits when you aren't around. Sure, you're a hulking killing machine but they aren't.<br /> <br /> Now add Hosts, Choirs, etc. Monster of the Week quickly ceases to be that when the spider host is wearing your love one's face.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:25:27-08:00","id":431708,"title":"","content":"I love the mechanics and the book so far but I feel due to the word count it kind of feels like some of the explanations and rules where shoved in their by force. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, I do have questions that still need answering for Primal Urge, though I got to say that the mechanics for it are magnificent. And if anyone already beat me to these questions, then my bad. <br /> <br /> Can a werewolf decrease his/her PU? If so, how?<br /> <br /> The PU aging. Do werewolves stop aging when they have high PU? Does that still exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:37:22-08:00","id":431719,"title":"","content":"I pretty much agree with YOLF's post entirely. The book is great, but it really needed more word count and a couple fewer Idigam to make room for more information on different kinds of Prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:37:29-08:00","id":431720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431579#post431579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claire and I actually had a chat about those two back when we conceptualized them, and the similarity (having an analog for both of the legendary progenitors) was intentional. I don't recall offhand if we specifically discussed tribes or not, though.<br /> <br /> Still, one might strike better chords in someone's chronicle than the other (and, judging from comments I've seen here and on RPG.net, it looks like Claire's is the more popular! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), so that's something to keep in mind. Or, again to the best of my recollection as I don't have the thing in front of me at the moment, I don't think either of them are particularly powerful on their own. There isn't anything saying you couldn't use both in a chronicle back behind the scenes. I mean, what would it do to the Forsaken if it appeared like both their Mother and their Father were no longer distant (or dead), but instead, actively engaging with the world?<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts, which may or may not appeal to anyone's given game. But maybe it'll strike up some ideas, so that's good at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've gotten a few comments, but I think the Deceiver Lune is really damn awesome. And yes, we did communicate, and I think they're plenty different enough that concluding they both simply want tribes of their own is flawed. <i>Lul'Aya </i>wants to be Father Wolf, not just lord of one tribe. The Deceiver Lune is cool not because of its power but because of its purpose, and its means of reaching its goals. Its effects are more insidious in the fervor they inspire, and I think that's cool. The Deceiver Lune's coming is not the avalanche itself, but the falling snowflake that sets off the avalanche. It's a lot more difficult to pin it down and by the time packs are facing this would-be tribe, things have already gotten very, very dangerous indeed.<br /> <br /> So I say bravo, and I personally look very much forward to using the Deceiver Lune in my games\u2014always have!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:39:35-08:00","id":431725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431708#post431708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The PU aging. Do werewolves stop aging when they have high PU? Does that still exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm keeping it no matter what the devs say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-07-2015, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:03:00-08:00","id":431750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431725#post431725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm keeping it no matter what the devs say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the devs have said anything to the contrary!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:12:17-08:00","id":431758,"title":"","content":"In the updates Stew mentions a bit about PU but didn't went deep into it. I know he said you can't raise your PU by feeding on another werewolf. And he went through the whole feeding and essence thing too. But as for what I'm curious, nope. Any clues that their is or did I miss something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:15:35-08:00","id":431763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431708#post431708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the mechanics and the book so far but I feel due to the word count it kind of feels like some of the explanations and rules where shoved in their by force.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I do have questions that still need answering for Primal Urge, though I got to say that the mechanics for it are magnificent. And if anyone already beat me to these questions, then my bad.<br /> <br /> Can a werewolf decrease his/her PU? If so, how?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the corebook, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The PU aging. Do werewolves stop aging when they have high PU? Does that still exist? </div> </div> </div>Look at the Field of Dogs Hunting Ground if you want some hints on that - if what Lycaon-Ur claims about his origins is true, then he's over 2000 years old. He's certainly several hundred years old at the minimum. Of course, you might not believe his claims, you might wonder what happens to a Primal Urge 10 werewolf over time anyway, and you might wonder whether he's a werewolf at all...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:16:13-08:00","id":431764,"title":"","content":"I don't think it has any way to go down. You buy it. It goes up, it stays up. Maybe you could make some crazy rite or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:48:51-08:00","id":431804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431708#post431708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the mechanics and the book so far but I feel due to the word count it kind of feels like some of the explanations and rules where shoved in their by force.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I do have questions that still need answering for Primal Urge, though I got to say that the mechanics for it are magnificent. And if anyone already beat me to these questions, then my bad.<br /> <br /> Can a werewolf decrease his/her PU? If so, how?<br /> <br /> The PU aging. Do werewolves stop aging when they have high PU? Does that still exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No. At least, not at present. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) We know of a couple of high-PU werewolves who are well over a hundred and are't about to lie down. Lycaon-Ur <i>might</i> be telling the truth, but he's a bit of a special case. Nobody knows the average natural lifespan of a werewolf at any PU, because they all die violently. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Certainly, I have no intention of saying &quot;Hey, even high-PU werewolves have to worry about old age&quot;, but at the same time I don't want to start setting out mechanics for ageing since that comes up so rarely in games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:51:07-08:00","id":431805,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling uratha either die relatively young or <i>really</i> sodding old.<br /> <br /> Like, they get to 100 there's not a lot that can put them down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T14:54:38-08:00","id":431806,"title":"","content":"I'm just trying to imagine the circumstances that would have to come together to <i>allow</i> a High Primal Urge werewolf to live for a long time. It seems like in most circumstances the ecosystem(spiritual or otherwise) would collapse after too much hunting*.<br /> <br /> I'm beginning to wonder why, exactly, the term bodhisattva is used to describe these predators.<br /> <br /> *Like, a few decades of constant predation, within the spans of weeks or days. Seriously, something's gonna fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:03:51-08:00","id":431811,"title":"","content":"Well clearly they don't hunt too much. Spirits eat each other all the time. By that point the werewolf is just part of the ecosystem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:30:17-08:00","id":431848,"title":"","content":"Primal Urge requires Siskur-Dah at increasingly frequent intervals as it rises. So they can't 'not hunt too much'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:36:45-08:00","id":431853,"title":"","content":"Tasty tasty Essence.<br /> <br /> High Primal Urge werewolves tend to have quite the impact on a region. They're movers and shakers, drivers of activity, their hunger and their need to hunt demanding that they not become sedentary or passive. They're the sorts to push Protectorates into attacks on powerful spirits that are causing trouble - not necessarily because they care so much about the trouble, but because they want to hunt <i>worthy</i> prey and consume the spirit to sate their hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:39:19-08:00","id":431860,"title":"","content":"Actually that raises something I wasn't too clear on. Do you need to go through the whole sacred hunt thing to eat a spirit for food?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:41:51-08:00","id":431876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431860#post431860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that raises something I wasn't too clear on. Do you need to go through the whole sacred hunt thing to eat a spirit for food?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, It was very unclear for me as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:44:42-08:00","id":431877,"title":"","content":"If you want to get Essence out of it (which is what a high Primal Urge werewolf needs to feed on) then yes, you need the Sacred Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:55:14-08:00","id":431902,"title":"","content":"So if they go more than 3 days without a proper hunt do they lose an essence for that and one for not eating properly or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:04:07-08:00","id":431932,"title":"","content":"They can draw Essence from Loci and cannibalism, so that can handle the feeding restriction.<br /> <br /> It does not fulfill the need for Siskur-Dah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:05:49-08:00","id":431934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431902#post431902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if they go more than 3 days without a proper hunt do they lose an essence for that and one for not eating properly or what?</div> </div> </div> </div> You loose one point of Essence each day for not feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:07:11-08:00","id":431936,"title":"","content":"If they are both not hunting <i>and</i> not feeding then yes, they will suffer the Essence loss from both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:14:57-08:00","id":431941,"title":"","content":"Alright, I think I get it now. <br /> <br /> What happens if they don't have any essence in their system? Is that when the starvation rules kick in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:33:16-08:00","id":431973,"title":"","content":"I was going to ask that as well. If a werewolf doesn't have essence in their system what happens to them? Do they go into a comma like in 1st Ed? And what about high PU werewolves, what happens to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:44:42-08:00","id":432000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431804#post431804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) No. At least, not at present. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) We know of a couple of high-PU werewolves who are well over a hundred and are't about to lie down. Lycaon-Ur <i>might</i> be telling the truth, but he's a bit of a special case. Nobody knows the average natural lifespan of a werewolf at any PU, because they all die violently. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Certainly, I have no intention of saying &amp;quot;Hey, even high-PU werewolves have to worry about old age&amp;quot;, but at the same time I don't want to start setting out mechanics for ageing since that comes up so rarely in games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool! Thanks Stew! I totally forgot about Lycaon-Ur's story. It is one of my personal favorite of the book. <br /> <br /> Well to be honest I was curious about this because I plan on making a game of ancient immortal (ageless) werewolves. With Dark Eras giving us amazing ancient eras I plan on making a chronicle for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:34:18-08:00","id":432026,"title":"","content":"Honestly I would get rid of the Eating Rules entirely. It's too similar to the penalties of not engaging the Siskur-Dar, specially for High Primal Urge Werewolfs. They basically have to engage in it everyday to hunt a spirit for Essence, instead of the time limit for doing the Siskur-Dar.(Unless they eat the meat of man or wolf of course, but that is against the Oath...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:42:05-08:00","id":432037,"title":"","content":"They can also satisfy their need for Essence through a Locus, as noted above, but then a high Primal Urge werewolf is probably going to end up grabbing the most potent Locus they can find to guzzle down its sustenance, which in turn means conflict because everyone <i>else</i> wants potent Loci too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:44:32-08:00","id":432039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432037#post432037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can also satisfy their need for Essence through a Locus, as noted above, but then a high Primal Urge werewolf is probably going to end up grabbing the most potent Locus they can find to guzzle down its sustenance, which in turn means conflict because everyone <i>else</i> wants potent Loci too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I forgot about it!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:45:40-08:00","id":432040,"title":"","content":"But, it still doesn't answer what would happen if a werewolf has no Essence in it's body,or having no Essence, can't find sustenance or doesn't engage in the Sacred Hunt.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:48:44-08:00","id":432060,"title":"","content":"A regular werewolf with no Essence is just a werewolf with no Essence - can't fuel their powers or do anything that requires it, but they're otherwise fine (I think).<br /> <br /> An elder werewolf with high Primal Urge and no Essence will, I believe, start to starve on the same basis as a regular werewolf who doesn't get any food (I think).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T19:17:59-08:00","id":432133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=431720#post431720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've gotten a few comments, but I think the Deceiver Lune is really damn awesome. And yes, we did communicate, and I think they're plenty different enough that concluding they both simply want tribes of their own is flawed. <i>Lul'Aya </i>wants to be Father Wolf, not just lord of one tribe. The Deceiver Lune is cool not because of its power but because of its purpose, and its means of reaching its goals. Its effects are more insidious in the fervor they inspire, and I think that's cool. The Deceiver Lune's coming is not the avalanche itself, but the falling snowflake that sets off the avalanche. It's a lot more difficult to pin it down and by the time packs are facing this would-be tribe, things have already gotten very, very dangerous indeed.<br /> <br /> So I say bravo, and I personally look very much forward to using the Deceiver Lune in my games\u2014always have!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah I'm looking forward to using all five of the idigam at some point, as well as possibly making others. I think they're all interesting. My comment about yours being more popular was based only on my impression of commentary I've seen - certainly nothing against it! Lul'Aya rocks socks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T01:25:28-08:00","id":432413,"title":"","content":"The book is fuckin' amazing. Werewolves got what they needed: more focus (and power). And to the one saying that werewolves 2e are weaker than B&amp;S...did you even read the book? XDDD<br /> I have only three main complaints:<br /> 1) The rules are sometimes not clear or scattered around in the book. I had to look at Reknown to understand some things of learning gifts, which wasn't included in the paragraph about gifts. This is one of the examples.<br /> 2) Hi, you need a rite (Sacred Hunt) to activate some of your BASIC AUSPICE abilities. Ah, did I mention that if you don't have that rite you suffer penalties for not going on a sacred hunt? I had to create a character starting with Sacred Hunt to ensure at least one of us had the rite.<br /> 3) So... all werewolves are ritualists? That's a bit WTF when I read it. Though rites itself are FANTASTIC and I love them. The fact that you can buy them in any order you wish, almost like merits, is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 03-08-2015, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T01:36:15-08:00","id":432414,"title":"","content":"Of course it's WTF. What book did you think you were reading? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:12:53-07:00","id":432434,"title":"","content":"Can anyone talk me about the new Totem rules? in the previous edition, they were little more than a xp sink hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:25:21-07:00","id":432444,"title":"","content":"If you have five pack members and each throws two merit dots into the pot they get a three experience benefit each, so that's a profit right there. Also the NPC wolf booded pack members can contribute so you'll some totem power for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:28:22-07:00","id":432447,"title":"","content":"But are the benefits the same as before, or have they been &quot;power-up&quot; too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:37:35-07:00","id":432449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432040#post432040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, it still doesn't answer what would happen if a werewolf has no Essence in it's body,or having no Essence, can't find sustenance or doesn't engage in the Sacred Hunt.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They starve, same as a werewolf who doesn't eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:39:13-07:00","id":432450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432447#post432447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are the benefits the same as before, or have they been &quot;power-up&quot; too?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can buy Merits, Skill Specialties, Skills and Attributes. These apply to every member of the pack, including Wolf-Blooded and human packmates. If you buy a dot of Strength, then every member of your pack gets stronger. If you buy a dot of Intelligence, every member of your pack gets smarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T04:39:47-07:00","id":432451,"title":"","content":"You get a number of experiences. You can use them to buy whatever you want, and the entire pack (humans, wolf blooded and werewolves, regardless of whether they possess the merit themselves or not) gets that trait. And you don't need to spend totem points on it, either. For a given number of points you get a set number of experiences and a set totem size. The totem gets an attribute dot per dot and a numina per four dots and you figure out it's rank from there. You could get a rank 5 totem with enough investment.<br /> <br /> Ninja'd, but I have just realised that that list doesn't include gifts, which makes sense given that the benefits now extend to characters unable to use them, but I can see how that could be considered a &quot;downgrade&quot; of sorts. I feel the other improvements make this more than worthwhile though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-08-2015, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:32:47-07:00","id":432611,"title":"","content":"Two questions:<br /> 1) Where it's said you have to perform the Sacred Hunt Rite to be able to use your Hunter Aspect? I saw some people saying it but didn't find anything about it the Hunter Aspect section.<br /> 2) For the purposes of Essence loss for not enganging in the Hunt does it mean you have to perform the Rite and then Hunt, or just hunt in general?<br /> (If you have to perform the rite for it it kinds penalises lone wolfs that don't know the rite or a pack that doesn't buy it. Instead of being a Rite you buy it would be better to be something every Uratha knows how to do by instinct then.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:00:46-07:00","id":432697,"title":"","content":"So I finally finnished all of the book and I can say that I really liked it. Werewolfs have become really sexy and dangerous predators, the whole book has a very visceral feel to it, it makes you want to get down in all fours and just hunt. It's unapologetically bloody and violent, the Auspices got really good writeups, you can really feel them as approach to the Hunt instead of just 'jobs&quot;.<br /> The Shadow feels much more organic and animalistc, you can really understand it more of an animal side of the world than you did in the previous editions. The inclusion of humans and wolf-blooded in the packs really added a lot to the dualist side of the Uratha, it helps drives the horror of it all, you have the people you consider family and around them you act like I a normal and caring human being, but to the ones outside if the needs arises they will just become prey, for them you will become a completely amoral monster.<br /> The only complaint I have it that I agree it could have used a bit less of the Idigam(and God they are terryfing by themselves and their creations), instead of giving long write-ups of different ones and their activities they could have been shorter and use the espace to talk more about the other prey like the Hosts.<br /> To sum the second edition in only one word: <b>savage</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:14:27-07:00","id":432708,"title":"","content":"I have another complaint as well.<br /> Why isn't Teen Wolf listed as suggested reference? The show is a perfect exemple of the new diverse format of a pack!!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T11:18:32-07:00","id":432804,"title":"","content":"I did personally suspect it early in development, but while I think they definitely improved Forsaken in terms of rules and some aspects of the setting, it still very much lacks what Requiem in both incarnation managed: Being a good game about it's supernatural protagonists with unique aspects and flairs to enhance this without blocking off too much of the spectrum of stories about its main characters.<br /> <br /> There are a few glimpses of improvement for that, the thing with wolfblooded with their different tells is nice, though I think a good couple of it could have worked better if it also extended to full werewolves.<br /> <br /> I want to echo some of the points brought up by others and add a few of my own:<br /> <br /> -Siskur-Dah: I think it is suitable for werewolves to make a rite out of the hunt, it also seems good to give it some nice benefits, but...<br /> When it comes to the point where werewolves literally cannot go without and that so much is tied into a single rite, for me, it feels weird. It feels weird if something so integral about werewolves is about a ritual they have to learn and enact. The problem is that this time, the sacred hunt is so deeply rooted in the whole system that it is too difficult to remove it or fundamentally change it if it does not suit one.<br /> -Unclearness: I have to say I am rather disappointed here. Plain errors in the pdf aside (swapped pages, parts of text replaced with something garbled), some things are said too vaguely (or spread over the book too much) to be easily comprehended and I find it especially jarring since previous editions were actually better there. Making one overview chapter that covered all the facets of the game roughly and then go into the details later worked before, it did not work that well this time.<br /> -Gauru: It improves over the previous Gauru in actually being useful, but it is now so very much all or nothing. I still am not really fond of the regenerate all no aggravated damage bit...<br /> And also, the facet meant to make Gauru less of a berserk engine of destruction fails to really deliver (it still make sit behave just the same way in combat, I would rather have it be something that made the whole super regeneration, down and dirty combat and berserk factor switch off).<br /> -Individual Powers: Some do feel a bit too &quot;gamey&quot; to me, or on the other hand overspecific. It is not too bad, but some gifts and similar felt not really as interesting and thematic as others.<br /> -Tribes: The problem still is that tribes feel a bit off with the whole structure of werewolf society. Giving them their specific prey did not really help me like them better. I would have preferred a bigger focus on heritage from one of the firstborn instead and establish clear themes different from the auspices. It is unfortunate because the Apocalypse tribes, o matter their issues, at least did manage to give a useful extra dimension that &quot;made sense&quot; in the game world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, while this may be a weak impression so far, it does indeed seem a bit too strong on glorifying the aspect of hunting and killing and less of the coming to terms with being a monster which was more prevalent in the first edition.<br /> Granted, I was not happy with the first edition take either, but it seems to just have shifted from one overall mood I did not care for to another.<br /> I would so have liked a greater focus on a duality between the animal and the human side with the horror of breaking under that duality and having the conflict of what someone would do if he suddenly had all the power of being a powerful animal.<br /> I liked how they touched on that in Skinthieves.<br /> <br /> Maybe it is just that there are so many werewolf aspects, both from apocalypse and forsaken, which are too much beyond and above the commonality of werewolf stories to ever make it fit everyone's desires for a werewolf game, but I admit I had hoped for a bit more in that direction.<br /> There are some very nice touches and big, big improvements over the very messy rules from before, but most of my positive feelings come from my greater disappointment with the first edition than from the intrinsic merits of this one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T11:29:15-07:00","id":432817,"title":"","content":"To be fair all not engaging in the hunt does is make it so you lose one magic juice point a day. That's the same rate vamps lose it, and it never does them too much harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T11:51:48-07:00","id":432865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432817#post432817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair all not engaging in the hunt does is make it so you lose one magic juice point a day. That's the same rate vamps lose it, and it never does them too much harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with him in a lot of aspects, but I agree that the Hunting Rite being so central to the phsycology and activities of the Uratha and impacting so much in the Primal Urge should be instinctive and not learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T11:59:49-07:00","id":432875,"title":"","content":"True. <br /> <br /> Here's an idea. Cross out &quot;Siskur-Dah&quot; and write &quot;hunting&quot;. Any sort of hunt. You go out, kill a thing and eat it. Catching a pigeon counts. The Wolf Must Hunt. Nothing more, nothing less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:22:11-07:00","id":432920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432817#post432817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair all not engaging in the hunt does is make it so you lose one magic juice point a day. That's the same rate vamps lose it, and it never does them too much harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, correct me if I am wrong, as I am not very experienced with WtF, but I was under the impression Essence is generally harder to get than Vitae. For Vitae you have delicious two-legged Happy Meals running around everywhere! Essence requires a bit more search and even then is limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:30:19-07:00","id":432944,"title":"","content":"At some point I will write up a bit of explanation and examination as to why the Siskur-Dah is specifically a rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:36:13-07:00","id":432949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432920#post432920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, correct me if I am wrong, as I am not very experienced with WtF, but I was under the impression Essence is generally harder to get than Vitae. For Vitae you have delicious two-legged Happy Meals running around everywhere! Essence requires a bit more search and even then is limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence can be found everywhere Vitae can, if you're willing to take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:07:41-07:00","id":432997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432944#post432944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point I will write up a bit of explanation and examination as to why the Siskur-Dah is specifically a rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I have no problem with it being a Rite(it celebrates the part of them that are spirit after all), but being so central to what a Uratha is I think it should be something they can all intuitively perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:21:18-07:00","id":433013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432997#post432997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I have no problem with it being a Rite(it celebrates the part of them that are spirit after all), but being so central to what a Uratha is I think it should be something they can all intuitively perform.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an easy fix. Just give that right for free at character creation as part of the Werewolf template. I can't imagine very many players objecting to that house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:24:08-07:00","id":433021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433013#post433013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an easy fix. Just give that right for free at character creation as part of the Werewolf template. I can't imagine very many players objecting to that house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:28:34-07:00","id":433026,"title":"","content":"I really love the book. Obviously it could use some cleaning up but that seems to be what the errata gathering is all about.<br /> <br /> It's a shame stuff had to be cut for word count. But after seeing how the Idigam and their creations have been revamped, I can appreciate waiting for a more thorough retelling of the Pure and Bale Hounds and other shartha and enemies. As a storyteller I particularly like the whole 'Do what thou will' aspect. Put the Dread Powers you find appropriate on a monster, rather than working out a point system. And the monster creator system is something Werewolf has needed since the start. Plus while scattered about the book there's a lot of ideas and suggestions that open up opportunities for things beyond the Hunt, which is nice to have access to as a storyteller. As a player I like the 'feel' of the new book. Blood and Smoke had it too, but there's something more visceral about it. And there's very much an emphasis on keeping active and doing things, whether it's looking to pursue the hunt or understanding territory or dealing with spirits or packmates and keeping things balanced one way or another, which is nice for a player. I'm also glad they're continuing the trend of having bonuses like merits tied with their own story-based drawbacks, giving players more hooks to participate in.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and while I've never been interested in playing a wolf-blooded myself, as a storyteller I really appreciate the wide variety of Tells available, furthering options for storytelling. And I just flat out like them now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-08-2015, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:56:00-07:00","id":433084,"title":"","content":"You'll note that starting with the Sacred Hunt is already provided for in the game - all werewolves begin with 2 dots of rites, which is enough to buy Sacred Hunt. This might be due to being taught them by Tribal tutors, instinctive knowledge of the symbols and meaning, or other possibilities.<br /> <br /> The reason it's '2 dots of rites' and not 'all werewolves know the Sacred Hunt rite' is to provide more options to players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:59:08-07:00","id":433090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433084#post433084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that starting with the Sacred Hunt is already provided for in the game - all werewolves begin with 2 dots of rites, which is enough to buy Sacred Hunt. This might be due to being taught them by Tribal tutors, instinctive knowledge of the symbols and meaning, or other possibilities.<br /> <br /> The reason it's '2 dots of rites' and not 'all werewolves know the Sacred Hunt rite' is to provide more options to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Acrozatarim! If that and the explanations given on eating, I guess all my doubts have been cleared up!<br /> Now I can stop thinking and just let the wolf hunt!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:59:52-07:00","id":433092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433084#post433084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that starting with the Sacred Hunt is already provided for in the game - all werewolves begin with 2 dots of rites, which is enough to buy Sacred Hunt. This might be due to being taught them by Tribal tutors, instinctive knowledge of the symbols and meaning, or other possibilities.<br /> <br /> The reason it's '2 dots of rites' and not 'all werewolves know the Sacred Hunt rite' is to provide more options to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that, because its not really a rite you need every packmate to know. This way you can have one huntmaster in charge of calling Siskur-Dah, and everyone else is free to spend those dots on other things if they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:07:54-07:00","id":433104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433092#post433092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate that, because its not really a rite you need every packmate to know. This way you can have one huntmaster in charge of calling Siskur-Dah, and everyone else is free to spend those dots on other things if they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, my lot in the Paris game started with the Bone Shadow having Sacred Hunt, the Blood Talon having Hunting Ground and the Storm Lord having Banish and Totemic Empowerment.<br /> <br /> I fully expect the Blood Talon and Storm Lord to eventually pick up their own Sacred Hunts, just for the different benefits for their favoured prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:54:30-07:00","id":433177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433084#post433084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that starting with the Sacred Hunt is already provided for in the game - all werewolves begin with 2 dots of rites, which is enough to buy Sacred Hunt. This might be due to being taught them by Tribal tutors, instinctive knowledge of the symbols and meaning, or other possibilities.<br /> <br /> The reason it's '2 dots of rites' and not 'all werewolves know the Sacred Hunt rite' is to provide more options to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:01:05-07:00","id":433289,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that werewolves and Sin-Eaters style of magic have some eerie correlations going on now, between some similiatirities between Renown Brands(/Scars)/Gifts and Key/Manifestations and the syncretism of both Rites and Ceremonies.<br /> <br /> Urge to crossover rising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-08-2015, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:04:01-07:00","id":433294,"title":"","content":"Apparently one of the people who bought the 'do your own' expansion for Dark Eras added Sin-Eaters to Werewolf Vikings time period. But Sin-Eaters have always been similar to Uratha at their core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:06:56-07:00","id":433298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433294#post433294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently one of the people who bought the 'do your own' expansion for Dark Eras added Sin-Eaters to Werewolf Vikings time period. But Sin-Eaters have always been similar to Uratha at their core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes-I've commonly described Sin-Eaters as being at the crossroads between changelings and werewolves-but it's never been magic deep before on the werewolf side. Now it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:45:22-07:00","id":433481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=432875#post432875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True.<br /> <br /> Here's an idea. Cross out &quot;Siskur-Dah&quot; and write &quot;hunting&quot;. Any sort of hunt. You go out, kill a thing and eat it. Catching a pigeon counts. The Wolf Must Hunt. Nothing more, nothing less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reading the book again and it has pop up. The Primal Urge table only says Hunt Time but the description says:<br /> &quot;She also cannot spend long without the thrill of the Sacred Hunt, for fear of losing her predatory edge. The chart below sets out<br /> ow long she can go without being on the Siskur-Dah.&quot;<br /> Tough Siskur-Dah seens to be according to the glossary both a rite and a lifestyle, so it still muddy that the Essence loss of the hunting time means a time without hunting, or a time without the Sacred Hunting Ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T21:03:03-07:00","id":433558,"title":"","content":"I just have to say that I was sad to hear that the Pure would see a light treatment in the book because of limited word count available. However, having read the book now, I was delighted at just how much was packed into that limited space. I'm really impressed at how well done it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T21:21:00-07:00","id":433565,"title":"","content":"I wanna give a shout out to David A. Hill Jr., not only for Forsaken and Forgotten, but belatedly for Bowery Dogs. I love the way both of the settings take advantage of the idea of being forsaken and uses it to the fullest with people who were getting all the shit at times. It's a testament that my favorite thing about Tokyo, which has freaking <i>kaiju</i> to fight, is the struggle with Ainu identity for the Uratha. I just gotta take my hat off for both of these settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:26:39-07:00","id":433601,"title":"","content":"So I reread the First Change section of the book and it doesn't really say on how exactly a werewolf does it, rather it explains the experience. Does it just happen or is their something else now? Do you have to be Wolf Blooded in order to go through the First Change or can a regular human go through it as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:30:15-07:00","id":433604,"title":"","content":"It just happens.<br /> <br /> No comment on Wolf-Blooded or human thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:36:47-07:00","id":433609,"title":"","content":"Hmm...seems too vague. But I guess it can work for the player's own choosing and style then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T01:01:46-07:00","id":433659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433565#post433565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna give a shout out to David A. Hill Jr., not only for Forsaken and Forgotten, but belatedly for Bowery Dogs. I love the way both of the settings take advantage of the idea of being forsaken and uses it to the fullest with people who were getting all the shit at times. It's a testament that my favorite thing about Tokyo, which has freaking <i>kaiju</i> to fight, is the struggle with Ainu identity for the Uratha. I just gotta take my hat off for both of these settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw shucks. Thank you! Means a ton to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T01:38:30-07:00","id":433668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433294#post433294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently one of the people who bought the 'do your own' expansion for Dark Eras added Sin-Eaters to Werewolf Vikings time period. But Sin-Eaters have always been similar to Uratha at their core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure this was the create-an-era guy and not one of the 5k expansions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T03:53:56-07:00","id":433779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433558#post433558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have to say that I was sad to hear that the Pure would see a light treatment in the book because of limited word count available. However, having read the book now, I was delighted at just how much was packed into that limited space. I'm really impressed at how well done it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I tried to pack in as much stuff as I could, hook-wise and hint-wise, to make the Pure section in the Prey chapter more than just a rehash of existing material <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433601#post433601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I reread the First Change section of the book and it doesn't really say on how exactly a werewolf does it, rather it explains the experience. Does it just happen or is their something else now? Do you have to be Wolf Blooded in order to go through the First Change or can a regular human go through it as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to be a Wolf-Blooded to undergo the First Change.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T05:16:43-07:00","id":433806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433668#post433668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure this was the create-an-era guy and not one of the 5k expansions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's an expansion, but they got to pick their own expansion. I don't know if it's one of the 5k or 10k offhand, someone made a list in the Dark Eras questions thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:15:17-07:00","id":434383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=433779#post433779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to be a Wolf-Blooded to undergo the First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay, thanks.<br /> <br /> Though I still find it weird and silly that it just happens. Some random dude walking and next thing you know, poof, you're a werewolf. What the hell? Maybe I'll try the classic werewolf bite to make things more dramatic. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:18:32-07:00","id":434385,"title":"","content":"Being picked at random doesn't mean there's no warning or build-up. Even the people who become wolf-blooded don't do it as an instant change, it tends to happen later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:45:57-07:00","id":434414,"title":"","content":"I guess I just don't see it dramatic as vampire and changeling. Being embrace by force or some other reason. Taken away from your family &amp; friends and change into an alien being. Sounds pretty crazy and dramatic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:15:13-07:00","id":434450,"title":"","content":"You have a period of about a month where things steadily progress from being a little temperamental and weird oddities crop up to the world bending and twisting around you and having fight off the urge to rip someone's throat out whenever they bump into you, and all the while you're trying to figure out the answer to the question &quot;Am I going insane, am I falling apart, <i>what the fuck is wrong with me?</i>&quot; until it finally explodes and the <i>everything</i> is violated as it just all shifts, you included, thrashing through flesh and spirit and home and foreign places until you are spent, with the most insane feeling of calm and purpose settling into your muscles and bones as the moon smiles down on you with it's many, many faces.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, that's just Tuesday for most people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:19:51-07:00","id":434458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=434414#post434414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I just don't see it dramatic as vampire and changeling. Being embrace by force or some other reason. Taken away from your family &amp; friends and change into an alien being. Sounds pretty crazy and dramatic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow goes nuts around a <i>nuzusul</i> for as much as a month in advance of the First Change and unless you're quite lucky you <i>will</i> kill someone (possibly several someones) in the throes of your rebirth as a consummate hunter. <i>Signs of the Moon</i> includes an account from a werewolf who had her First Change in the middle of school. Steel Trap Mind got bitten in the middle of a massive riot and didn't Change until three weeks later and describes the sensation as &quot;[having] a shot of intense wrongness.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's without getting into the matter of what life gets like when a cult of wolf-shifters is waiting for you to crack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:40:03-07:00","id":434476,"title":"","content":"Really describing the first change as &quot;Some random dude walking and next thing you know, poof, you're a werewolf.&quot; is about as accurate as describing the embrace as &quot;some random dude in a bar and next thing you know, poof, some chick bit my neck&quot;. You're <i>turning into a giant fucking wolf monster</i>. YOU are the big scary dramatic thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:39:01-07:00","id":434582,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I see your point. I guess what I was trying to aim for was: what was or is the cause of your transformation? How exactly did you become a giant fuckin wolf monster? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:43:19-07:00","id":434588,"title":"","content":"The moment you were born. It's in your genes.<br /> <br /> It's like finding out you have Huntington's Disease, but possibly worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:10:39-07:00","id":434639,"title":"","content":"So basically genetics, just like in 1st Ed. I see. I thought it might have change in this new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:16:06-07:00","id":434650,"title":"","content":"Except if you get a Dramatic Failure in response to Lunacy you can become wolf-blooded and a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:20:04-07:00","id":434680,"title":"","content":"That's true. In 2e a bite <i>can</i> be the indirect cause of becoming a werewolf. It's just not a particularly reliable one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:45:02-07:00","id":434740,"title":"","content":"Though I personally like the classic werewolf bite, it makes things more interesting, as in &quot;you made me what I am!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:55:20-07:00","id":434752,"title":"","content":"Although humans probably have a bit of difficulty telling werewolves apart when they're all doggy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:03:52-07:00","id":434758,"title":"","content":"It's a doggy dog world lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:11:23-07:00","id":434763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=434740#post434740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I personally like the classic werewolf bite, it makes things more interesting, as in &quot;you made me what I am!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunacy kinda does that. To a point.<br /> <br /> See a Uratha change shape. <i>BLAM! </i>You're now wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> That's when things get weird...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:32:00-07:00","id":434816,"title":"","content":"Its a little thing, But I really love that werewolves can see angels and ghosts (and spirits) in twilight without a power. I might be having my pack be haunted by previous victims...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:40:31-07:00","id":434822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=434816#post434816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a little thing, But I really love that werewolves can see angels and ghosts (and spirits) in twilight without a power. I might be having my pack be haunted by previous victims...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026That's wolf-blooded with a particular Tell, else the first effect of Barghest makes no sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:27:30-07:00","id":435563,"title":"","content":"You're correct. Werewolves, by default, can't see angels and ghosts; they can see spirits in Twilight just fine, though. Barghest gives werewolves the ability to see anything death-aligned in Twilight (ghosts, mages using Death magic, etc).<br /> <br /> Note that Bone Shadows can <i>hurt</i> anything in Twilight with their Sacred Hunt benefits, although they gain no special benefits to sensing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:44:30-07:00","id":435693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=434740#post434740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I personally like the classic werewolf bite, it makes things more interesting, as in &quot;you made me what I am!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which to me is pretty boring, especially for werewolves. A Werewolf has to take responsibility for their actions, that is what being a werewolf is all about (at least to me - savage horror and all that)... blaming someone else for your problems is just passing the buck, in my opinion...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-10-2015, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:55:22-07:00","id":435700,"title":"","content":"There's a gift that give you the Moon Tainted Condition that is very close to the classic werewolf bite tough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:29:22-07:00","id":436271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=434740#post434740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I personally like the classic werewolf bite, it makes things more interesting, as in &quot;you made me what I am!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's more of a Vampire theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T16:18:11-07:00","id":436392,"title":"","content":"I feel the game has improved a lot more with the 2.E. That said though I feel there's still some hold over from 1E that should have been left behind such as flat bonuses, Long wait between rolls for powers. I also find the new regeneration rules a bit lacking. Considering how much more deadly 2E WoD is due to auto successes, the regeneration doesn't really strike me as a creature capable of coming back from anything.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head few things I would house rule for my games:<br /> Auspice benifits will no longer be based on flat bonuses. The Cahalith Auspice ability with give +/- equal to Glory. The Elodoth will be able to use it's death rage ability equal to renown, Irraka can open doors equal to cunning and the Rahu can ignore conditions that hinder combat for a number of turns equal to Purity.<br /> <br /> Any gifts that have a flat bonus would be house ruled the same.<br /> <br /> I would house rule regeneration to be 1/1 with Primal Urge. so 1 bashing at PU , 2 at PU 2, 3 at PU 3, ect, ect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:00:56-07:00","id":436427,"title":"","content":"The lethal regeneration per turn is exactly the same as what they were capable of in 1e until they hit Primal Urge 7, and it's cheaper to boot. And the answer to anything requiring more than that is &quot;go gauru&quot;.<br /> <br /> Admittedly towards the upper end they're left with a massive amount of essence per turn and a distinct lack of things to do with it. Vamps can blood boost to crazy levels, but lacking any such innate abilities (or gifts, now that savage might is gone) You're sort of left wondering what exactly you would need to be doing to spend 15 essence at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:15:09-07:00","id":436439,"title":"","content":"I have to admit if I was going to change anything other than 'adding 300 more pages to detail everything' an increase in the healing per primal urge would be it. While I wouldn't go for a 1:1 rate, I'd probably have 1B only at first dot, 2B at second, then increase every two dots after until 6B at 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:24:06-07:00","id":436548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=435693#post435693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which to me is pretty boring, especially for werewolves. A Werewolf has to take responsibility for their actions, that is what being a werewolf is all about (at least to me - savage horror and all that)... blaming someone else for your problems is just passing the buck, in my opinion...</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. I get my taste from movies and some books. I like the whole personal horror and inner perspective of the character who deals with it, especially being new. I like how a simple person going with their usual life is suddenly attack and change by force by a reckless or selfish werewolf. That person was probably having a good life and is angry that he/she lost it and has to commit horrible acts in order to survive it's new life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T21:04:48-07:00","id":436643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=434822#post434822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026That's wolf-blooded with a particular Tell, else the first effect of Barghest makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quit bringing me down with facts, man!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=435563#post435563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're correct. Werewolves, by default, can't see angels and ghosts; they can see spirits in Twilight just fine, though. Barghest gives werewolves the ability to see anything death-aligned in Twilight (ghosts, mages using Death magic, etc).<br /> <br /> Note that Bone Shadows can <i>hurt</i> anything in Twilight with their Sacred Hunt benefits, although they gain no special benefits to sensing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, crap, You're right, I misread page 95.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":".  Snark. 03-11-2015, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T21:59:00-07:00","id":436714,"title":"","content":"One question I have about the lore of the spirits, specifically the tribal totems and the Maejiln, what rank are they now? Dihar(Incarna) or Ilusah(Celestine)? The book is a bit confusing about this part of the Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T22:01:56-07:00","id":436717,"title":"","content":"That information about the Tribal Totems is vague, likely on purpose. The Maeljin are called Diharim in their sidebar, which means Rank 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T04:48:09-07:00","id":436902,"title":"","content":"Page 181, 'The \u201cweaker\u201d Ilusah are spirits like the Firstborn; patrons of entire tribes. Mother Luna and her brother Helios are the best-known greater Ilusahim.'<br /> <br /> Personally I like that the Firstborn totems have more presence in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T05:39:01-07:00","id":436919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=436902#post436902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I like that the Firstborn totems have more presence in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I particularly like to play up the very personal connection to Tribal totems in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me that I haven't yet done that in my Paris game. I'll probably emphasise it in the second story arc once the pack go beyond trying to secure their own turf and start looking beyond their borders at the wider landscape of Uratha packs and alliegances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T06:27:57-07:00","id":436966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=436902#post436902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 181, 'The \u201cweaker\u201d Ilusah are spirits like the Firstborn; patrons of entire tribes. Mother Luna and her brother Helios are the best-known greater Ilusahim.'<br /> <br /> Personally I like that the Firstborn totems have more presence in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaker Ilusah(Rank 7) seens to still be able to sent totems forth into the world, so that they can still interact I guess. Souless Wolf(if he even is a Firstborn) seens to have been downgraded, serving mere Diharim(the Maeljin).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:00:16-07:00","id":437058,"title":"","content":"He's only downgraded if they keep the same concept of him as from Blasphemies, as servant of the Maeljin. And that's also providing ALL Maeljin are Diharim.<br /> <br /> @Acrozatarim I like that a lot, in one of our games there was supposed to be this mixed up atmosphere in the background, because two of the Firstborn were supposed to be making a deal of some sorts and they chose our city as a sort of neutral ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:29:39-07:00","id":437072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=436902#post436902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 181, 'The \u201cweaker\u201d Ilusah are spirits like the Firstborn; patrons of entire tribes. Mother Luna and her brother Helios are the best-known greater Ilusahim.'<br /> <br /> Personally I like that the Firstborn totems have more presence in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I missed that. My bad.<br /> <br /> Though, I'm all for the Tribal Totems having a greater presence in the word and more direct connection to their tribes too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:52:34-07:00","id":437138,"title":"","content":"It's not a good thing if Basra is any indication. The First Born are like gods upon the land a wreck hell with the world via their influence. Fenris is slowly driving all his Talons insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:58:09-07:00","id":437146,"title":"","content":"I think the problem there isn't so much that it's there as much as it's <i>staying</i> there. Some of the other examples suggest they've appeared briefly to tackle big threats with less upsetting of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:58:18-07:00","id":437147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=437138#post437138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a good thing if Basra is any indication. The First Born are like gods upon the land a wreck hell with the world via their influence. Fenris is slowly driving all his Talons insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>That it's probably not ever an unambiguously good thing is the interesting part!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:00:39-07:00","id":437149,"title":"","content":"If Fenris has found his mate and that's the purpose of the ghost wolves there (to be the new tribe) the that hisil is going to be wrecked once they eventually move on. Unless it becomes a den. You'll be looking at creation and destruction on a biblical scale, with something like psychopathic armies and super crazy red cross working the land.<br /> <br /> edit: which would make for an interesting pure anti firstborn campaign, or even a standard campaign of trying to placate/move on the two earth shakers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:52:49-07:00","id":437711,"title":"","content":"I was looking over the Oath of the Moon section and I can't help but feel that Cleave to the Human just doesn't fit anymore. Don't get me wrong I'm glad that we're done with the problematic issues that Unihar created but that one bit of the Oath is now out of place. The other sections of the oath have multiple paragraphs explaining interpretations, reasons, and applications to the characters but the Cleave the to the human part is just one simple paragraph that honestly reads like it was made up on the fly to find some way to keep the oath the same.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better changed to &quot;Cleave to the wolf and human&quot; Keeping in mind that you are parts of both and both sides are equally important","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:58:59-07:00","id":437718,"title":"","content":"I think it works fine. It says &quot;cleave to the human&quot; not &quot;cleave <i>with</i> the human&quot;, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T00:25:03-07:00","id":438138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Inevitable</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=437711#post437711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking over the Oath of the Moon section and I can't help but feel that Cleave to the Human just doesn't fit anymore. Don't get me wrong I'm glad that we're done with the problematic issues that Unihar created but that one bit of the Oath is now out of place. The other sections of the oath have multiple paragraphs explaining interpretations, reasons, and applications to the characters but the Cleave the to the human part is just one simple paragraph that honestly reads like it was made up on the fly to find some way to keep the oath the same.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better changed to &quot;Cleave to the wolf and human&quot; Keeping in mind that you are parts of both and both sides are equally important</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from imagery, wolves are irrelevant to werewolves. They're optional extras.<br /> <br /> Born from humans, creatures of half spirit, werewolves need to nourish their spirit side by visiting the Hisil, and balance this with their physical selves by staying close to the humanity they came from. They just happen to look like wolves when they transform, and have patronage from wolf-like spiritual patrons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:47:19-07:00","id":438587,"title":"","content":"Hi guys! I new but i need sign up on forum just to share my view of the book!<br /> <br /> I really amazed with the book overall,com we got a misunderstanding on kuruth part And some pages are swaped, but this can be easily fixed i believe, i really like the new predator perspective now, i always complained about this back in WTA ( you can always go red talon lupine but i think you guys got my point), now we can feel more like a real werewolf, i really think we dont need any new material of the pures so soon, what we got is enough to run then on a game( we can still use other books right?)<br /> <br /> Auspice is awesome too, now i dont need read signs of moon to get the whole pitcture, and all of them get their part on the hunt.<br /> <br /> I read somewhere people on foruns are worried about gauru regeneration, after i play test with my Group i noticed its not a big deal after all, ir all depends on the way you hunt( or got hunted), if you imagine a scenario where two gaurus fight a endless match on gauru really it will not work, but in a real hunt it make sense in the way it is.<br /> <br /> Sorry for poor grammar guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:37:10-07:00","id":441893,"title":"","content":"A thought that occurs to me as I attempt to get my usual RP group interested and invested in Werewolf for the first time:<br /> <br /> I wish they had severely cut down on the use of First Tongue. It creates a language barrier that some of my friends find very off-putting. I understand the reasons for its inclusion, and I enjoy it personally, but I am stuck having to consider the perspective of 'this thing is detrimental to my ability to use this product.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:03:55-07:00","id":441910,"title":"","content":"It fits the game. Perhaps the glossary should have been placed more front and center but while the ranks might be confusing, everything else is a made up concept anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:32:22-07:00","id":441955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=441910#post441910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It fits the game. Perhaps the glossary should have been placed more front and center but while the ranks might be confusing, everything else is a made up concept anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't the ranks so much as the entire concept of having to pick up on fragments of another language to make sense of what the book is talking about. Or hell, the book could have refrained from using First Tongue as frequently when describing things and stuck to more plain language; that would make my players less irritable about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:57:15-07:00","id":441987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=441955#post441955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't the ranks so much as the entire concept of having to pick up on fragments of another language to make sense of what the book is talking about. Or hell, the book could have refrained from using First Tongue as frequently when describing things and stuck to more plain language; that would make my players less irritable about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But everytime they used a First Tongue term for the first time(and a lot for other times too) they provided the translation immediately at the side.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T17:09:20-07:00","id":441992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=441987#post441987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But everytime they used a First Tongue term for the first time(and a lot for other times too) they provided the translation immediately at the side.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That in no way lessens their irritation.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong: I like First Tongue. I find it fun.<br /> <br /> But my foremost concern remains the individual tastes and preferences of my group, and my ability to get them to buy into the game and become invested. First Tongue is an obstacle in this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 03-14-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:52:33-07:00","id":442878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=437718#post437718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it works fine. It says &quot;cleave to the human&quot; not &quot;cleave <i>with</i> the human&quot;, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue isn't that it's not about mating anymore. As I said I'm glad that's gone from 2E. The issue is that it feels out of place in the book now with it's new write up. The new Harmony rules make it pretty clear about the theme being a balance between your two halves and yet &quot;Cleave to the human&quot; is a complete 180 on that. The part of the oath should read that you need to cleave to both your halves to be a perfect Predator, not just one half.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:16:40-07:00","id":442931,"title":"","content":"&quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; is the first tenet and ties you to spirit. &quot;Cleave to the human&quot; is there to act as balance and bring you close to flesh. Or maybe is another instance of Luna being a crazy motherfucker and messing with his adopted children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T13:36:50-07:00","id":443052,"title":"","content":"If it's about maintaining harmony half the oath should pull you one way and half the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T14:16:38-07:00","id":443112,"title":"","content":"Nah, it also works if you have the same number of tenets that go one way and the other as long as the remaining tenets are neutral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:37:43-07:00","id":443507,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else think the rule about a werewolf's prey getting a bonus to the Lunacy roll is backwards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T21:34:00-07:00","id":463123,"title":"","content":"So somehow I'm only just now getting to the Wolf-Blooded and <i>omigawdguys </i>I love them <i>sooooo</i> much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T23:51:06-07:00","id":463170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=443507#post443507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think the rule about a werewolf's prey getting a bonus to the Lunacy roll is backwards?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, I actually really like it. It reminds me of fight or flight responses. I essentially see Lunacy as an actual weakness that can be overcome with rites, lunacy making social connections outside of the pack difficult. As well as a tool that can be used to scatter the rest of the herd and isolate a particular target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T23:13:35-07:00","id":517699,"title":"","content":"Neglected to mention something that I appreciate 2e making near-explicit:<br /> <br /> Areas of human activity having a higher Gauntlet means the local Shadow bears less aesthetic resemblance to Earthly reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T06:13:24-07:00","id":517897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=517699#post517699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neglected to mention something that I appreciate 2e making near-explicit:<br /> <br /> Areas of human activity having a higher Gauntlet means the local Shadow bears less aesthetic resemblance to Earthly reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see where it made that explicit, but coming from you I'm sure it's there.<br /> <br /> Regardless, that <i>is</i> a great idea. I was worried that areas of high human activity were barren Spirit wastelands, but it makes more sense that they'd be less like deserts and more like twisted areas of deadly still ephemeral remains. Not to mention they'd be crawling with hungry spirits devouring each other, and every locus being like a military fortress surrounded by hungry invaders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T08:59:02-07:00","id":518097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=517897#post517897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't see where it made that explicit, but coming from you I'm sure it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 72, &quot;The Hisil&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once through the Gauntlet, the Hisil awaits. Depending on where the traveler crossed over, the Shadow can seem very similar to the material world or obviously different. <b>The thinner the Gauntlet in a location, the more the worlds resemble one another.</b> In deep wilderness, far from humanity, the Shadow is only shaped by the simple feelings of animals and the environment. In the heart of a city, the crowds stir the Shadow into chaos. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:50:26-07:00","id":518301,"title":"","content":"so im skirming through the book now. <br /> <br /> Only 4 illustrations of Ron Spencer, YES! still 4 more than there should be in any book but i take the good where i can find it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Im curious do the ghost child were removed from 2E? The offspring of 2 werewolves?<br /> <br /> There is still that whole tennet of &quot;Garou shall not kill Garou&quot; never like it, and never made sense to me but it is easily removable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:06:10-07:00","id":518313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518301#post518301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious do the ghost child were removed from 2E? The offspring of 2 werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were removed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:06:15-07:00","id":518314,"title":"","content":"Yes, unihar are gone. <br /> <br /> Also how does &quot;don't kill each other&quot; not make sense? We've got a society to run here and werewolves are inherently violent creatures. We do kinda need it to not come crashing down around our ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:06:28-07:00","id":518315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518301#post518301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so im skirming through the book now.<br /> <br /> Only 4 illustrations of Ron Spencer, YES! still 4 more than there should be in any book but i take the good where i can find it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Im curious do the ghost child were removed from 2E? The offspring of 2 werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they removed the <i>unihar</i>. There's a thread discussing it...<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508576-on-the-removal-of-unihar\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is still that whole tennet of &quot;Garou shall not kill Garou&quot; never like it, and never made sense to me but it is easily removable.<br /> </div> </div> </div>It's Uratha. Or werewolf. Or The People if you wanna get fancy.<br /> <br /> But yes, it's still there. But like you said, easy enough to remove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T14:44:32-07:00","id":518443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518314#post518314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, unihar are gone.<br /> <br /> Also how does &quot;don't kill each other&quot; not make sense? We've got a society to run here and werewolves are inherently violent creatures. We do kinda need it to not come crashing down around our ears.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On many fronts really. For starters Uratha at least in 1st edition had a very loose society, it gave the impression that most pack were islands on themselves. And for what im seeing in 2e they follow through that, like removing the rites of contrition and funeral one that really dont made sense in how the setting was presented.<br /> <br /> So when Uratha fight the pure what then? they suposelly beat them up and let them go? Sure the drama can be sweet at that but in my experience most players try to find a way to cheat it or we just agree to remove it because well, its werewolf a game in which you are a killing machine, a killing machine that just deliver non lethal blows to their sworn enemies is weird.<br /> <br /> Thats just my taste and experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:24:22-07:00","id":518509,"title":"","content":"The Pure are just as resilient when it comes to healing as the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> The Oath of the Moon is what Luna wants. Even if you don't remove it, nothing stops you from killing other werewolves except for them being hard to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:33:49-07:00","id":518521,"title":"","content":"The thing about fighting the pure is that a lot of the time you can go &quot;hey, it was either me or them&quot; and most other forsaken will go &quot;yeah, that sounds legit&quot; even if that wasn't actually true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:47:01-07:00","id":518529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518443#post518443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On many fronts really. For starters Uratha at least in 1st edition had a very loose society, it gave the impression that most pack were islands on themselves. And for what im seeing in 2e they follow through that, like removing the rites of contrition and funeral one that really dont made sense in how the setting was presented.<br /> <br /> So when Uratha fight the pure what then? they suposelly beat them up and let them go? Sure the drama can be sweet at that but in my experience most players try to find a way to cheat it or we just agree to remove it because well, its werewolf a game in which you are a killing machine, a killing machine that just deliver non lethal blows to their sworn enemies is weird.<br /> <br /> Thats just my taste and experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason it's worded &quot;The People don't kill The People&quot; and not &quot;Werewolves don't kill Werewolves.&quot; There's a lot of room for interpretation. Do the Pure count as The People? They sure don't count the Forsaken among The People, so when they kill your packmates are you just going to turn the other cheek and say &quot;the oath forbids it&quot; or are you going to look for an excuse why it's not <i>technically</i> against the oath? There's a whole tribe now that considers other werewolves their sacred prey (the Blood Talons), so there must be at least <i>some</i> cases where it's acceptable, right? Those kinds of moral questions create dramatic tension, which is exactly why the writers included it in the Oath and left it ambiguous who does or doesn't count as The People. And, of course, with the way Harmony works now, the occasional violation of the Oath can actually bebeneficial and help maintain balanced Harmony. You don't want to do it <i>too much</i> or the Blood Talons might decide<i> you</i> don't count as The People anymore, but that's just more potential for drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:51:51-07:00","id":518533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518509#post518509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure are just as resilient when it comes to healing as the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> The Oath of the Moon is what Luna wants. Even if you don't remove it, nothing stops you from killing other werewolves except for them being hard to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i would say degerations roll would stop one from doing so.<br /> <br /> sure socially i dont mind being a taboo thing in <b><u>some</u></b> situations. But being pure or not you still have degeneration roll (or its automatic now maybe, i havent reach that chapter yet).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518529#post518529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, of course, with the way Harmony works now, the occasional violation of the Oath can actually bebeneficial and help maintain balanced Harmony. You don't want to do it <i>too much</i> or the Blood Talons might decide<i> you</i> don't count as The People anymore, but that's just more potential for drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>This raises a good point actually, i would need to see how it goes into play but i could see a group saying &quot;Guys we are to spirit now, we should off some pures!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T16:42:45-07:00","id":518568,"title":"","content":"There's not really degeneration rolls, just breaking points towards the spirit and the flesh. So you're not going to lose your character for repeatedly breaking the Oath of the Moon, though some more civic-minded aspirant of Luna might decide to hold you in contempt. Or try to make sure you don't have a character to keep.<br /> <br /> Even in first edition, though, you weren't exactly supposed to try and maintain the highest Harmony possible. You're supposed to follow your character, and the story, and some characters were bent more towards a lower Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-18-2015, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:25:04-07:00","id":518676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518443#post518443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when Uratha fight the pure what then? they suposelly beat them up and let them go? Sure the drama can be sweet at that but in my experience most players try to find a way to cheat it or we just agree to remove it because well, its werewolf a game in which you are a killing machine, a killing machine that just deliver non lethal blows to their sworn enemies is weird.<br /> <br /> Thats just my taste and experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no drama without moral quandaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:33:49-07:00","id":518683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518676#post518676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no drama without moral quandaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Everything you complain about just means tension and drama, which is pure joy for my groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T18:45:54-07:00","id":520313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=518676#post518676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no drama without moral quandaries.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everyones game is different, in my experience players dont usually go for the kill but when they go is not a dramatic to say &quot;of yeah, you gonna loss harmony&quot;. Players groan, PC groans and the drama was resolved RP instead of mechanically but its a moot point as charlaquin pointed out how now it could be benificial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T01:35:35-07:00","id":520916,"title":"","content":"Oh, it can almost <i>always</i> be beneficial if you do it right. Want to kill a dude, but you're north of 5 so a breaking point towards flesh is bad? Eat them. Because that's <i>always</i> towards spirit. <br /> <br /> The balance of harmony can now be maintained with precisely distributed corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:03:29-07:00","id":521934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=520916#post520916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it can almost <i>always</i> be beneficial if you do it right. Want to kill a dude, but you're north of 5 so a breaking point towards flesh is bad? Eat them. Because that's <i>always</i> towards spirit. <br /> <br /> The balance of harmony can now be maintained with precisely distributed corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you're ok with the potential social consequences of being a cannibal. If just killing werewolves wasn't enough to get the Blood Talons after you, eating them definitely will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:06:04-07:00","id":521937,"title":"","content":"I don't know if eating humans counts as cannibalism, though other werewolves is pretty obvious. The book states repeatedly werewolves aren't humans. I've had some weird luck in that regard, I've eaten like half a dozen people and my Harmony hasn't dropped from it yet. Though it has from other things.<br /> <br /> Strange luck aside, I'm really digging the new Harmony. I don't like the looming threat of, 'Play a certain way or we'll take your character from you.' Even though I could never really see my characters dropping below 2-3 at the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:10:08-07:00","id":521944,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously you need to make sure you don't get <i>caught. </i>I was speaking from a purely Harmonic point of view. <br /> <br /> Just make sure you dispose of the bodies in such a way that the bite marks aren't obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:13:17-07:00","id":521948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=521944#post521944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, obviously you need to make sure you don't get <i>caught. </i>I was speaking from a purely Harmonic point of view.<br /> <br /> Just make sure you dispose of the bodies in such a way that the bite marks aren't obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Black Earth, Red Hunger</b> is such a great facet for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:57:43-07:00","id":521970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=521948#post521948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Black Earth, Red Hunger</b> is such a great facet for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Meninna are goddamn terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:03:58-07:00","id":521973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=521937#post521937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if eating humans counts as cannibalism, though other werewolves is pretty obvious. The book states repeatedly werewolves aren't humans. I've had some weird luck in that regard, I've eaten like half a dozen people and my Harmony hasn't dropped from it yet. Though it has from other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. Same as eating actual wolves. Think of a mule eating a horse or an ass.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:07:27-07:00","id":521977,"title":"","content":"I thought when it mentioned wolves it was just shorthand for werewolves. Since wolves aren't really common animals, and tend to be endangered as it is. Though I guess you could go to a zoo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429027-e2-my-thoughts-please-share-your-own?p=521970#post521970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Meninna are goddamn terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>They need to be. Not to diminish the threat of the other sacred prey, but you can always do aggravated to a human or werewolf, and I think Claimed might be close enough. Even if they aren't, Claimed and Spirits have bans and banes. The shartha don't have any weaknesses, and the only gifts that target them out are mostly for identifying and keeping them out of an area.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose if one is puppeteering a person you could manage the massive damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-20-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:13:37-07:00","id":521988,"title":"","content":"I think they use the term cannibalism because it's shorter than not-exactly-cannibalism-but-there's-no-equivalent-concept-in-real-life-so-it'll-have-to-do. <br /> <br /> The way to think of it is that werewolves are both humans and wolves. So they are both human and not-human at the same time. And any mystical link they have with humans also applies to wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:18:21-07:00","id":521994,"title":"","content":"So, started reading this tonight, spotted Alice Springs is in there. &quot;Southwest of town there\u2019s the Gap \u2014 an American military base with 10-foot fences, machinegun nests, spotlights, and guards.&quot; Jeez, -10 points <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually, as a local, the &quot;Gap&quot; is Heavitree Gap (pronounced Heavy Tree Gap, its the point where the Todd River cut through the ranges and is also the spot where the highway south heads through the ranges), Pine Gap is the military base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}